 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S444-009\", \"clauses\": {\"create\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F02\", \"template\": \"Create a pattern that starts at {first_term} and uses the rule: {rule}. Which sequence shows this pattern?\", \"reasoning\": \"F02 opens with the task verb Create and its own sentence asks for a pattern, so it addresses the clause. The fault that fails the item (see overall) does not remove the ability to produce this clause.\"}, \"increasing_decreasing\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"Which sequence correctly shows {v} {pattern_label} starting at {first_term} and following the rule: {rule}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 names the property through the pattern_label domain, whose three members include increasing pattern and decreasing pattern. Those labels can be produced for a direction clause. The article and rule coupling faults are separate and are recorded in failing_families.\"}, \"patterns\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F02\", \"template\": \"Create a pattern that starts at {first_term} and uses the rule: {rule}. Which sequence shows this pattern?\", \"reasoning\": \"F02 asks the learner about a pattern, which is the object the lc names.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F02\", \"F03\", \"F04\", \"F05\", \"F06\", \"F07\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Create a pattern that starts at {first_term} and uses the rule: {rule}. Which sequence shows this pattern?\", \"Start at {first_term} and create {v} {pattern_label} with the rule: {rule}. Which pattern did you create?\", \"Start at {first_term} and use the rule: {rule_description}.\", \"The sequence that follows the rule at every step is {answer}.\", \"Which sequence correctly shows {v} {pattern_label} starting at {first_term} and following the rule: {rule}?\", \"You want to create {v} {pattern_label} where the rule is: {rule}. Which sequence correctly creates it?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"Three faults. (1) Independent slots: in F03, F06 and F07 the pattern_label domain (decreasing pattern, increasing pattern, repeating pattern) and the rule domain (F08: Add or Subtract, step 1 to 5) are declared as separate generator choices with no derived_from_values link, so a problem can state an increasing or decreasing rule for a repeating pattern, or Add with a decreasing pattern. The repeating pattern label is also outside this lc, which asks only for increasing or decreasing patterns. (2) The article slot v (members a and an) is declared as a separate choice, not tied to pattern_label, so a learner can be shown an article that does not match its noun (for example a before increasing). (3) Keyed answer and hints are not coupled to the question: F09 answer draws from its own observed list with derived_from_values answer only, and F02, F03, F06 and F07 use first_term but not the answer. F04 and F05 print rule_description and answer as separate generated values. A problem can therefore key a sequence that does not start at first_term or follow rule, and F05 can state that such a sequence follows the rule. F07 also renders up to 20 words in its sentence (for example with an increasing pattern and a one-digit step), over the lc's sentence_max_words of 18. Not a fault on its own: sequence and rule are not in cumulative_vocab but are not in NOT_YET_KNOWN either, so they are outside the gate and were not counted. Also not counted: the answer list shows only step sizes 1 to 4, while the rule domain allows step 5 and Add 4, which never appear in the observed answers; this is coverage, not a text fault.\"}",
